# Purity and determinism

`src/core` is pure. No I/O, no `Date`, no `Math.random`, no module-level
mutable state, no `process`. Everything the engine needs is in the
`GameState` it was handed.

Randomness is **state as data**: `seedRng(seed)` produces an `Rng`, and
`nextInt(rng, n)` returns `[k, rng2]`. There is no hidden generator. Two runs
from one seed and one tap list are byte-identical, on any machine, forever.

`act` and `getView` never mutate their arguments. They return new state. The
acceptance suite deep-freezes inputs and will catch you.

`eslint.config.js` enforces the mechanical half of this — `Math.random`,
`new Date`, `Date.now`, `process`, `console`, and `new Set/Map` are all
restricted syntax inside `src/core`. The lint is a floor, not the rule.

> "load" means validate, not read from disk. A `src/core` function takes the
> parsed value; the caller does the reading.
